<title>USA: ADR REPORT - Christmas holiday cools ADR market.</title>
<headline>ADR REPORT - Christmas holiday cools ADR market.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The fast approach of the Christmas holiday brought trading in American Depositary Receipts, or ADRs, to a near halt.</p>
<p>&quot;Things are stable but quiet with really little going on,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>In Latin American ADRs, Telmex was up 1/8 at 31-7/8, Vitro SA fell 1/8 to 5-3/8, and YPF SA slipped 1/8 to 24-3/4.  </p>
<p>European ADRs similarly were lackluster in late morning activity, with oil stocks off after this week's rally and telecommunications stocks slightly higher.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a particularly quiet day,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>British Petroleum was in line with Monday's close at 138-7/8. Royal Dutch Petroleum Co gained 1/8 to 171.</p>
<p>British Telecommunications gained 3/8 to 66-5/8 and Vodafone Group Plc climbed 1/8 to 41-1/4.</p>
<p>((-- Patricia Willens, 212-859-1727))</p>
